Sign it only when the technical documentation is complete and the conformity assessment is done. The structure follows Annex V of the EU Cyber Resilience Act. Point 3 says "manufacturer" where Annex V says
"provider": Articles 13(12) and 28 make the manufacturer draw up the declaration and take responsibility for it.
CE marking: for software, put the CE marking on this declaration or on the product's website (in a part of the site
consumers reach easily and directly), and only once the conformity assessment has shown that the requirements are
met, before the product is placed on the market (Articles 13(12), 30(1) and 30(3)). -->
